    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee stands and the driver is paid SGD 3.20, being 80% of that fee under POL-NS-07. The ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and the figure 3.20 sits in both money fields because POL-GEN-03 requires it on a driver-compensation ruling; it is the amount this ruling moves, not a second payment and not a refund to the rider, whose charge stands.\n\nThe fee. The trip record shows the driver arrived at the ION Orchard PHV bay at 18:44:30 and cancelled at 18:52:45 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. The GPS trace is complete (100% coverage, no gaps, weight 1.0) and contains 40 qualifying in-radius fixes inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius, so POL-NS-02 is satisfied and POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) hold. Limb (d) holds: the driver terminated the trip on a no-show code at 18:52:45, with no boarding event recorded anywhere.\n\nThe dwell, which is the point the rider argues. The rider is right about the raw arithmetic: no single continuous hold reaches 300 seconds. The two holds are 170 s (18:44:45 to 18:47:35) and 185 s (18:49:35 to 18:52:40), and the longest is 185 s. But POL-NS-06(i) is the rule this policy gives for how that dwell limb is measured where a kerb restriction is in force: it permits separate in-geofence intervals within one pickup attempt to be summed, provided the driver never went more than 300 m from the pin and a qualifying advisory covered the road and the waiting window. Both conditions are met. The driver's furthest point during the 18:47:35 to 18:49:35 loop was 179.0 m, inside the 300 m leash, and EV-ADVIS-00214-01 is a populated LTA KERB_RESTRICTION (full-day bus lane, no stopping, waiting or picking up, 17:00 to 20:00 on Orchard Turn) whose geometry covers the pickup road and whose active window covers the whole waiting period. The rider's contrary argument, that the exception cannot apply because the driver was able to hold the kerb for 185 s and that POL-NS-06(i) cannot enlarge the word 'continuous' in POL-NS-01(c), is rejected: POL-NS-06(i) is precisely the provision that states whether separate stretches are summed, and the advisory's own terms (vehicles holding the kerb will be moved on) together with the driver's 18:47:50 message that the marshal moved him on show that holding position was not lawfully possible. Accumulated dwell is 355 seconds against the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum, a surplus of 55 seconds, so POL-NS-06 does not displace the charge.\n\nOther clauses. POL-NS-03 is not engaged: the zone has one registered pickup point, so the pin-ambiguity precondition is absent, and the driver's stationary fixes are inside the arrival radius rather than outside it. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: the driver replied at 18:47:50, 90 seconds after the rider's 18:46:20 message, inside the 120-second window, and limb (c) is affirmatively failed because the rider's device never came closer than about 690 m to the pin (zero qualifying rider fixes) against the 150 m LARGE_VENUE presence radius. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: at the 18:44:30 marker the driver was not more than 300 m from the pin and not travelling at 15 km/h or above, so the marker is not false and the waiting clock is not recomputed against him. POL-NS-08 is not engaged: the 4.00 fee equals the greater of the 4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone fee and the 4.00 RYDE_X tier fee, and every artifact in the bundle is COMPLETE at weight 1.0.\n\nDriver compensation and escalation. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of the 4.00 fee, 3.20, with the residual 0.80 retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2 of 118 completed trips is 0.017 (below 0.08). No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0, so there is no repeat-pair pattern; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below 3; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; and no deciding fact rests on impaired evidence. The rider's request for escalation is therefore refused, because the applicability of POL-NS-06(i) is not genuinely open on this record. No referral fires: POL-NS-05(ii) has no application because the arrival marker is not false.\n\nConfidence. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact, the GPS trace, the trip record, the traffic advisory, the fare breakdown and the driver profile, carries weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and confidence is set at 0.90. No context-only profile field (rating, account_age_days, lifetime_trips, cancellation_rate, prior_no_show_flags and the like) was used as a ground of decision."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

