    "explanation": "Outcome: the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee stands, and the driver is paid SGD 3.20 compensation (80% of the fee under POL-NS-07). amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd because on a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling the amount field carries the same figure the ruling moves, not a rider refund (POL-GEN-03).\n\nDRIVER — accepted. Arrival and dwell are verified on your own trace and record. EV-GPS-00214 (weight 1.0) places you inside the 120 m ION Orchard arrival radius from 18:44:45, 15 s after the EV-TRIP-00214 (weight 1.0) 'arrived' marker at 18:44:30, and the trip is terminated by you at 18:52:45 coded RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event, so POL-NS-01 limbs (a), (b) and (d) hold. On dwell, the trace shows two in-geofence holds — 170 s (18:44:45–18:47:35) and 185 s (18:49:35–18:52:40) — separated by a single loop in which you stayed 179 m from the pin, inside the 300 m leash. EV-ADVIS-00214-01 (weight 1.0) is a populated LTA KERB_RESTRICTION (full-day bus lane, Orchard Turn, 17:00–20:00, marshals active, vehicles holding the kerb moved on) whose geometry covers the pickup road and whose window covers the whole waiting period. POL-NS-06(i) therefore permits the two intervals to be summed: accumulated dwell is 355 s against the 300 s LARGE_VENUE minimum, a 55 s surplus, not a shortfall. The arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05 (you were stationary at the marker, first qualifying fix 15 s later, never at 15 km/h). No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the charge: POL-NS-03 fails because the zone has a single registered pickup point and your stationary fixes are inside the 120 m radius; POL-NS-04 fails because you replied within 120 s and the rider's device never came within 690 m of the pin; POL-NS-06 does not fire because there is no shortfall. The SDG 4.00 line reconciles exactly with fee_schedule.resolution_rule — the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X tier fee (4.00) — so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. POL-NS-07 is satisfied: the anti-farming check reads only no_show_terminations_30d (2, below 4) against completed_trips_30d (118, ratio 0.017, below 0.08), so the 20% retention does not apply and you receive 3.20.\n\nRIDER — your points are answered together and rejected. The five-minute minimum is not required to be one unbroken stand where a kerb restriction made holding unlawful: deciding the limb applies the rule another clause gives about it, and POL-NS-06(i) expressly allows separate stretches to be summed on exactly this advisory. The effective dwell is 355 s, so the shortfall case in POL-NS-06 never arises and the rider's whereabouts (properly, that the rider was not present) is beside the point. There is nothing genuinely open to escalate: no two admissible artifacts contradict each other, disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both sides, no_show_disputes_30d is 1, the anti-farming check is clear, and every artifact is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so POL-NS-09(a)–(e) are all unmet and the platform-wide 0.70 floor is not approached. Your account of a car wandering about is not supported: the chat log and the trace show one enforced loop off the kerb with a return to the same bay.\n\nAll bundle artifacts carry weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes, so no POL-GEN-02 discount applies and the ruling rests on evidence at full weight. The driver's counterparty statement carries no weight multiplier and is read as context only. No clause produces a referral (POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival record, POL-RD-06(c) and POL-RD-09(4) are all inapplicable), so referrals is empty."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

