o repeat-pair history (both counterparty counters are 0), no anti-farming trip and a rider 30-day no-show count of 1, and confidence is above the 0.70 floor. The applicability of POL-NS-06(i) is not genuinely open.\n\nOther checks. POL-NS-05: no false arrival marker — at the 18:44:30 marker the driver was stationary and well within 300 m. POL-NS-03: no wrong-entrance case — the driver's stationary fixes fall inside the arrival radius and the zone has a single registered pickup point, so the clause's premise is absent. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: the rider's 18:46:20 message was answered by the driver at 18:47:50, 90 seconds later and inside the 120-second window, so limb (b) fails, and limb (c) is affirmatively failed on admissible fixes (the rider's device never came closer than 690.7 m to the pin against a 150 m radius, with zero qualifying rider fixes). POL-NS-08: no limb is engaged — no clock skew (marker 15 seconds from the nearest fix), 100 per cent coverage with no gap, five chat messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count, and the $4.00 cancellation fee equals the greater of the $4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone fee and the $4.00 RYDE_X tier fee. Every artifact carries weight 1.0, so no POL-GEN-02 discount applies.\n\nOutcome. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full ((a) arrived event, (b) 40 qualifying in-radius fixes, (c) effective dwell 355 s ≥ 300 s, (d) cancelled at 18:52:45 on RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event and after the dwell elapsed) and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. The $4.00 cancellation fee therefore stands, and under POL-NS-07 the driver is compensated at 80 per cent of it: $3.20 of $4.00. The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2 of 118 completed trips is 0.017 (below 0.08). The emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION because compensation is paid, with amount_sgd carrying the same $3.20 figure as driver_compensation_sgd, the fee itself being left in place; the only profile fields used are the two POL-NS-07 names.",
